Z||000004||mshill||09-26-2000||02:10 AM||||I have been doing some research on the net and found the 3.4L upgrade for the S-10 trucks in the GM Performance website.  That says (for the trucks anyway) that the 3.4 is a direct boltin for the 2.8 and induction and exhaust is maintained.<P>The other thing is that 2.8/3.1 aluminum block.  It's already bossed for the starter on either side.  If I only had $2700 bucks just laying around.  Here's the dilema... Lottery tickets or 3.4L upgrade... lottery or house payment... lottery or well, you get the idea.<p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||80's BOY||09-26-2000||12:54 PM||||my 3.1 runs well with the factory fuel setup. i only changed the regulator to an adjustable one.<P><BR>85 Special GT<BR>Special Paint<BR>Special lowering springs<BR>Special 3.1 stroker<BR>Special passenger (when she rides along)<BR>Special 16inch rims with extra special tires<BR>Special "High Output" gas additive<BR>Special air horns to honk at those Special babes on the beach!!<P>Now isn't THAT special!! :-)||||reg||12
