Z||000007||Cooter||09-26-2000||09:26 PM||||3.4 with stock F/P and 3.4 injectors- too rich at idle and full throttle. Runs fine, but could stand to be a little cleaner though. Maybe a little less fuel pressure could help?||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-27-2000||12:45 AM||||thank's 86se.....||||reg||1
Z||000009||mshill||09-27-2000||02:42 PM||||Cooter, so with the 3.4 injectors it's too rich, have you tried the 2.8 injectors?  So, if you got an adjustable fuel pressure regualtor you would be turning the pressure down?  <P>I also just got off the phone with George from the FieroShop and he suggested 305 injectors with the adjustable regulator.<P>The more I find out, the more confused I get.<P>GM says stock is OK.<BR>Cooter says too rich with 3.4 injectors.<BR>FieroShop says us 305 injectors.<P>HELP!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||09-27-2000||07:37 PM||||By mistake, I am using stock everything with my 3.4.  It does seem to be starving for fuel.  I am getting 24# injectors and J. Wynmans 3.4 chip.  Not sure about the adj. fuel pressure regulator.  I guess I will wait until I get the injectors and chip.<P>BTW, I am not setting any codes with the 2.8 stuff, and I have noticed remarkable gas mileage....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||3
Z||000011||Black88GT||09-27-2000||07:39 PM||||<BR>p.s. 305 injectors are the same as 3.4 injectors.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||09-27-2000||08:22 PM||||The only time I noticed mine was rich was by the computer readings being at the limits of operation. It ran OK, but I wanted more than just OK, so the tinkering began. I don't know if 2.8 injectors would be enough fuel, but it may be worth trying with a regulator. I did not think of that.||||reg||1
Z||000013||88formula||09-27-2000||08:55 PM||||ED Parks told me he uses 2.8 injectors on his own personal 3.4 fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Old Lar||09-27-2000||09:28 PM||||Twin Lakes puts in new HP injectors for his 3.4 conversion and uses existing fuel rail.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Lunapark||09-29-2000||05:39 AM||||Ed Parks did my conversion. I purchased the 3.4 S-10 Crate motor for $1500.00 from Vancover, BC. through a dealership.  Ed tells me that he used 3.4 rebuilt injectors on my car. That the 2.8 injectors will starve the car for Fuel at about 5000rpm. The car currently has an idle problem but other than that, the car is very very quick and responsive. I did not use an adjustable fuel regulator according to Ed. He said that the car didn't need one. I have not had any fuel problems when driving the car only an IAC problem that I am currently working on. If any one has any questions about the install let me know. <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000016||RedOktober||09-29-2000||10:19 AM||||just a thought for you:<BR>After much research it has been found that there are several different formulae used to determine injector size. It appears that most of the various formulae in use are basically identical, with only 2 real variables, being whether or not an 80% duty cycle is accounted for and what the desired Brake Specific Fuel Consumption (BSFC) should be. This is the formula with the correction based on the duty cycle: <BR> <BR>  <BR>          Flow rate (lbs/hr) = Max Hp x BSFC / no. injectors x duty cycle<BR> <BR>         <BR> BSFC = 0.45 - 0.55 for naturally aspirated engines <BR>  <BR> <BR> 0.55 - 0.65 for forced induction engines<BR>  <BR> <BR> Conversion from lbs/hr to cc/min = lbs/hr x 10.515 <BR> <BR> <BR> Simplified max Hp x 1.807 (nat) <BR>Simplified max Hp x 2.136 (turbo)<BR> <BR>From <A HREF="http://www.haltech.com" TARGET=_blank>www.haltech.com</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater)||||reg||1
Z||000017||ThatRickGuy||09-29-2000||09:04 AM||||"That the 2.8 injectors will starve the car for Fuel at about 5000rpm. "<P>okay, now truthfully, how often do us fiero daily drivers run the engine up to or beyond 5k? Sure every once and a while ya hit WOT to clear traffic on interstate or on an on ramp, but still... If you're looking to save money, I'd say hold onto your 2.8 injectors. people are using that set up and are happy, and GM runs engines rich. Better rich and slow then lean and detonating, atleast for the dealership, that way, they have less of a chance to see your car again.||||reg||1
